# Visual Quality Gate

Before finalising any visual or front-end change, review whether it improves the coherence of the whole site, not just the local component.

Check:
- typography hierarchy
- spacing rhythm and consistency
- alignment and proportions
- image prominence and cropping
- desktop/mobile balance
- consistency with the site's existing editorial tone

Refine rough or merely acceptable solutions before stopping.

Do not introduce isolated visual ideas that look interesting on their own but weaken the overall character of the site.

Do not proactively suggest additional redesign ideas, new style directions, or broader visual changes unless the user asks for them or the current solution would otherwise remain visibly weak.
